  eventID: EscEventTwo
  dialogueLines:
  - "Why are you still pressing it? I just told you that doesn\u2019t do anything."
  - "You\u2019re still pressing Escape? I thought I made myself clear."
  - "The player pressed Escape again. Didn\u2019t I just say that wouldn\u2019t work?"
  - Again? Really? Escape still does nothing.
  - "Why keep pressing it? The narrator already explained that it\u2019s useless."
  - "The player seems convinced Escape will eventually do something. It won\u2019t."
  - You pressed it again. For what purpose? Nothing is going to happen.
  - Still trying Escape? The narrator is starting to think this is deliberate.
  - "The player has pressed Escape yet again. Apparently, one explanation wasn\u2019t
    enough."
  - "Escape does nothing. I\u2019ve said this already. Please stop pressing it."
  canRepeat: 1
